/*!
\page page_stetrhit StEtrHit

\ref StEtrHit represents a single reconstructed hit in the Endcap Tracking (ETR) prototype
detector.  The ETR is a small-scale forward tracking prototype with three radial layers and 12
azimuthal sectors.  All geometry is packed into the inherited <tt>mHardwarePosition</tt> word
using the formula <tt>section + 100*layer + 10000*sector</tt>.

\see StEtrHitCollection

\section sec_etrhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
StObject
└── StMeasuredPoint
    └── StHit
        └── StEtrHit
\endverbatim

Hits are collected in \ref StEtrHitCollection.

\section sec_etrhit_geometry ETR Geometry

| Parameter | Range | Description |
|-----------|-------|-------------|
| Layer   | 0–2  | Radial layer index (3 layers). |
| Sector  | 0–11 | Azimuthal sector (12 × 30°). |
| Section | 0–29 | Pad section within a layer–sector. |

\section sec_etrhit_members Data Members

\ref StEtrHit adds <b>no persistent data members</b> beyond those inherited from \ref StHit.
Geometry is encoded entirely in the inherited <tt>mHardwarePosition</tt>:

- <tt>UInt_t mHardwarePosition</tt> — <tt>section + 100*layer + 10000*sector</tt>.
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionError</tt> — Fixed sentinel <tt>(0,0,9)</tt> cm. <em>Not a measured uncertainty.</em>
- <tt>Float_t mCharge</tt> — Deposited charge (ADC counts).
- <tt>Int_t mId</tt> — Hit identifier.
- <tt>Int_t mIdTruth</tt> — Geant track ID (simulation only).
- <tt>UShort_t mQuality</tt> — Charge fraction from <tt>mIdTruth</tt> (percent).
- <tt>UChar_t mFitFlag</tt> — Non-zero if used in a track fit.
- <tt>UChar_t mTrackRefCount</tt> — Number of tracks referencing this hit.
- <tt>UShort_t mFlag</tt> — Hit status flag bitmask.

\section sec_etrhit_methods Key Methods

- <tt>int section() const</tt> — Pad section index (0–29): <tt>hardwarePosition() % 100</tt>.
- <tt>int layer() const</tt> — Radial layer (0–2): <tt>(hardwarePosition()/100) % 100</tt>.
- <tt>int sector() const</tt> — Azimuthal sector (0–11): <tt>(hardwarePosition()/10000) % 100</tt>.
- <tt>StDetectorId detector() const</tt> — Returns <tt>kEtrId</tt>.

Inherited from \ref StHit:

- <tt>StThreeVectorF position() const</tt> — Hit position in STAR global frame (cm).
- <tt>float charge() const</tt> — Deposited charge.
- <tt>unsigned int hardwarePosition() const</tt> — Raw packed geometry word.

\section sec_etrhit_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StEtrHit does not use a custom memory pool.  Objects are heap-allocated.  Ownership
transfers to the framework on insertion.
\warning Do <b>not</b> <tt>delete</tt> \ref StEtrHit pointers obtained from the collection.

\section sec_etrhit_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StEtrHitCollection* etrColl = event->etrHitCollection();
if (!etrColl) return;

const StSPtrVecEtrHit& hits = etrColl->hits();
for (const StEtrHit* hit : hits) {
    int sector  = hit->sector();   // 0–11
    int layer   = hit->layer();    // 0–2
    int section = hit->section();  // 0–29
    float charge = hit->charge();  // ADC counts
    StThreeVectorF pos = hit->position(); // STAR global (cm)
}
\endcode

\subsection subsec_etrhit_ctor Constructing an StEtrHit

\code{.cpp}
StThreeVectorF pos(x, y, z); // global position (cm)
StEtrHit* hit = new StEtrHit(pos, /*sector=*/3, /*layer=*/1,
                              /*section=*/12, /*charge=*/150.f);
etrColl->addHit(hit);
\endcode

*/
